# The Dockerfile builds from the repo root. Keep the context small and never
# let a host node_modules (wrong platform, wrong versions) shadow the one
# `npm ci` builds inside the deps stage.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
dist
out
build
.git
.github
.archive
.vercel
.claude
coverage
libs/db/src/generated
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The root .npmrc pins `script-shell=bash`, which exists ONLY so npm scripts
# survive Windows — npm there defaults to cmd.exe, which cannot parse `lsof`,
# `${VAR:-default}` or an inline `FOO=bar` prefix. These images are
# node:24-alpine, whose /bin/sh is busybox ash: already a POSIX shell, and with
# no bash on PATH at all. Copying the file in therefore breaks every npm script
# in the build with `spawn bash ENOENT` — which is exactly how the 8cccd77
# build failed at `npm run db:generate`.
#
# Excluded rather than answered with `apk add bash`: the container never had the
# cmd.exe problem this file solves, so carrying a shell in the image to satisfy
# a Windows workaround is fixing it in the wrong place. If a real build-time npm
# config is ever needed (a private registry token, say), add that file under a
# different name rather than un-ignoring this one.
.npmrc
